  <data name="Reset_PlaybackTitle.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Playback and output</value></data>
  <data name="Reset_PlaybackText.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Backend, devices, every backend setting, conversion and decoders return to their defaults (WASAPI following the Windows default device).</value></data>
  <data name="Reset_PlaybackConfirm" xml:space="preserve"><value>Output goes back to WASAPI following the Windows default device, and every backend setting, conversion and decoder choice to its default. The library, statistics and interface settings stay.</value></data>
  <data name="Reset_InterfaceTitle.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Interface</value></data>
  <data name="Reset_InterfaceText.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Language, what closing the window does, the queue panel, the tray notice and the first-run guide return to their defaults.</value></data>
  <data name="Reset_InterfaceConfirm" xml:space="preserve"><value>The language follows Windows again after a restart; closing the window minimizes to the notification area; the queue panel closes; the tray notice and the first-run guide count as not shown.</value></data>
  <data name="Reset_LibraryTitle.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Rebuild the library</value></data>
  <data name="Reset_LibraryText.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Reads the tags and covers of every file again and rebuilds the albums. Play statistics and playlists stay.</value></data>
  <data name="Reset_LibraryConfirm" xml:space="preserve"><value>Every file in every library folder is read again in the background; a large NAS library can take an hour or more. Play statistics, playlists and the folder list stay.</value></data>
  <data name="Reset_CoversTitle.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Cover cache</value></data>
  <data name="Reset_CoversText.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Deletes the generated cover thumbnails; they are made again when shown.</value></data>
  <data name="Reset_CoversConfirm" xml:space="preserve"><value>The generated cover thumbnails are deleted and made again as covers are shown. Music files are not touched.</value></data>
  <data name="Reset_AllTitle.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Reset everything</value></data>
  <data name="Reset_AllText.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>Back to a new installation: settings, the library with its folder list, play statistics, playlists, the cover cache and the logs are removed. Music files are not touched.</value></data>
